अभिगंतृ a. One who approaches or
has intercourse (with a woman);
one who understands &c.

अभिगूर्त p. p. Approved of;
destined for an offering; uttered
(with praise).

अभिगूर्तिः f.
1 Song of praise;
constant desire or thought;
Rv. 1. 162. 6.
--2 Effort, exertion.

1 Injuring, plotting
against, harm, cruelty, oppression;
Ms. 8. 271; Ki. 11. 21.
--2 Abuse;
censure.

अभिनंद् {c1c} P. (rarely Ā.)
1
(a) To rejoice at or in, exult over,
be glad or satisfied;
आत्मविडंबनामभिनंदंति K. 108; Dk. 75. (b) To
[]
celebrate (with rejoicings^1 &c.);
महोत्सवेन मज्जन्माभिनंदितवान् K. 137;
नाभिनंदति न द्वेष्टि Bg. 2. 57.
--2 To
congratulate, hail with joy, welcome, greet;
एनां परिष्वज्य तातकाश्यपेनैवं अभिनंदितं
Ś. 4; तापसीभिरभिनंद्यमाना शकुंतला
तिष्ठति ibid., 5, 6, 7; अभिनंदितागमेनषु
समीरेषु K. 49, 63; अभिनंद्य ब्रवीति
Mv. 2 says (writes) after compliments;
R. 2. 74, 3. 68, 7. 69, 71;
30; 16. 64; 17. 15, 60; Y. 1. 332.
--3 To rejoice at, approve, praise,
applaud, commend; यो रत्नराशीनपि
विहाय अभिनंद्यते Ś. 2; अतस्ते
वचो नाभिनंदामि ibid. do not approve;
तद्युक्तमस्या अभिलाषोऽभिनंदितुं Ś. 3;
श्रूयंते परिणीतास्ताः (कन्यकाः)
पितृभिश्चाभिनंदिताः 3. 24; नाम यस्याभिनंदंति
द्विषोपि स पुमान्पुमान् Ki. 11. 73; 4. 4;
with न reject; R. 12. 35.
--4 To care
for, like, desire or wish for, respect,
delight in (usually with न in this
sense); नाभिनंदति केलिकलाः Māl. 3;
नाहारमभिनंदति K. 61; Dk. 159;
आर्यपुत्रस्यैव मनोरथंसपत्तिमभिनंदामि Ve. 2
wish or desire; नाभिनंदेत मरणं
नाभिनंदेत जीवितं Ms. 6. 45, H. 4. 4.
--5
To bless, grant success to; U. 5. 28.
--Caus. To gladden, delight.
[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.

अभिनंदनीय --नंद्य pot. p. To be
rejoiced at, praised, or applauded;
काममेतदभिनंदनीयं Ś. 5; R. 5. 31.

